From: Dima Weber <diepress@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 03:50:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] common/hash.c: guard the SM3 wrappers with CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(SM3)

hash_init_sm3(), hash_update_sm3() and hash_finish_sm3() call sm3_init(),
sm3_update() and sm3_final() from lib/sm3.c, which tools/Makefile never
links, so mkimage fails to link with undefined references to them. Only
their registration in the hash_algo table is guarded by
CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(SM3); guard the three definitions the same way.

Upstream: Not submitted, buildroot uboot-tools packaging fix for 2026.07
Signed-off-by: Dima Weber <diepress@gmail.com>
---
--- a/common/hash.c
+++ b/common/hash.c
@@ -144,6 +144,7 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+#if CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(SM3)
 static int __maybe_unused hash_init_sm3(struct hash_algo *algo, void **ctxp)
 {
 	struct sm3_context *ctx = malloc(sizeof(struct sm3_context));
@@ -171,6 +172,7 @@
 	free(ctx);
 	return 0;
 }
+#endif
 
 static int __maybe_unused hash_init_crc16_ccitt(struct hash_algo *algo,
 						void **ctxp)
